3. Prints the JSON array of those coordinates to stdout.
4. Builds an orthogonal adjacency graph of the green cells, checks whether the green region is a single connected component, and – if the number of green cells is ≤ 12 – attempts a brute‑force search for a Hamiltonian cycle. It then prints either the found cycle (as a list of coordinates) or a brief explanation why none exists.

